=== attack audit — v4 vs heuristic on W0Base
  100 episodes, win_rate 0.810, 28.4 turns/ep

  attack rate                 1073/2817   0.381 [0.363,0.399]   creatures sent / could have attacked
    reference would send       883/2817   0.313 [0.297,0.331]   same denominator: the size of any over/under shoot
    reference (CA) would send   734/2817   0.261 [0.245,0.277]
  attack-optimality            704/1070   0.658 [0.629,0.686]   UPPER BOUND: includes no-choice combats
    ...where a choice existed   704/1070   0.658 [0.629,0.686]   the honest one
  attack-optimality (CA)       707/1070   0.661 [0.632,0.688]   reference charges for the crack-back

  score gap (myopic)         2802 over 1070 combats
  score gap (CA)             3114
  missed lethal              2   (own category, never a gap)
  errors UNDER / OVER        178 / 180   (sent fewer / more than ref)
  truncated subsets/replies  0 / 0
  combats with no choice     0   (MATCH there is the position's)

  cost: policy search 0 ms total, 0.00 ms/combat; audit 42706 ms (instrument, not play)
  nodes: 0k resolve() calls, 0 per combat

  READ WITH: the reference is one combat deep and prices at zero
  the fact that an attacker cannot block next turn, so it
  over-credits attacking. A rise in attack-optimality alongside
  a rise in attack rate is partly tautological; the CA row and
  the UNDER/OVER split are what separate them.
